    "title"             "Knox Relay"
    "description"       "Server-side bridge mod for remote server management. Exports game state, inventory snapshots, player positions, progression and live character vitals, and processes item delivery and money deposit queues via file-based JSON communication."
    "changenote"        "[h1]1.9 — The rest of the Build 42 API corrections[/h1]\n[b]Fixed[/b]\n[list]\n[*]Skill progress called getTotalXp and getXpForLevel on the value returned by getXP, which is a plain number rather than an object to ask further questions of. Progress now comes from the perk's own getTotalXpForLevel thresholds, so the XP bars finally move.\n[*]Profession was read with getProfession, which does not exist. The descriptor holds a CharacterProfession object; its name is read off that.\n[*]A worn slot can hold something that is not clothing — a backpack being the usual case — and holes, bite and scratch defence exist only on clothing. Asking a bag for them raised once per bag, per heartbeat. Worn non-garments are still listed, with those figures left at zero.\n[*]An empty-table check used next(), which PZ's Lua runtime does not provide at all. Body temperature raised on every heartbeat as a result, and the whole panel was lost.\n[/list]\n[b]Notes[/b]\nTogether with 1.8 this clears the character export of Build 41 assumptions. Every method the mod calls on a game object has now been checked against the shipped classes rather than against memory, and the test stubs define only methods the engine really has — a call the game does not support fails in testing instead of once a minute on a live server. Servers on 1.7 or 1.8 are treated by the web dashboard as not having the feature, since both wrote heartbeats full of defaults rather than readings."
}
